01:53:40.740 --> 01:53:44.310
So ultimately, you become the stronger, better person

2566
01:53:44.310 --> 01:53:45.810
because of your pain.

2567
01:53:45.810 --> 01:53:49.080
Yeah, and I've had some people ask me things like,

2568
01:53:49.080 --> 01:53:51.580
well, what if nothing's really happened to me

2569
01:53:51.580 --> 01:53:54.600
to where it's like, allowed me to see certain things,

2570
01:53:54.600 --> 01:53:55.730
it's like, I know they're there,

2571
01:53:55.730 --> 01:53:56.700
but nothing's really happened

2572
01:53:56.700 --> 01:53:58.390
to push me into that place that's like,

2573
01:53:58.390 --> 01:54:00.910
really bad to where I need to figure this out?

2574
01:54:00.910 --> 01:54:04.650
And it's a great question, and I don't necessarily know

2575
01:54:04.650 --> 01:54:06.170
that it has to be that way.

2576
01:54:06.170 --> 01:54:08.040
I think, what we--
Makes it easier,

2577
01:54:08.040 --> 01:54:09.620
it makes it way easier.

2578
01:54:09.620 --> 01:54:11.510
The thing, people ask me that question,

2579
01:54:11.510 --> 01:54:12.970
I'm like, I don't know what to tell you

2580
01:54:12.970 --> 01:54:14.510
because like, I just was in so much pain

2581
01:54:14.510 --> 01:54:17.220
I didn't feel like I had any other choice.

2582
01:54:17.220 --> 01:54:20.350
That choice is available to all of us at any moment,

2583
01:54:20.350 --> 01:54:22.560
it's just harder to make that choice

2584
01:54:22.560 --> 01:54:24.290
when you're not suffering.

2585
01:54:24.290 --> 01:54:26.080
'Cause who wants to do that kinda work?

2586
01:54:26.080 --> 01:54:28.160
Suffering does lead you--
if you feel like

2587
01:54:28.160 --> 01:54:30.990
you don't need to, it's like, I got shit to do.

2588
01:54:30.990 --> 01:54:32.363
You'll continue to.

2589
01:54:33.500 --> 01:54:36.650
And so I guess the only thing that I could really think

2590
01:54:36.650 --> 01:54:39.393
to say to someone in that position is like,

2591
01:54:42.000 --> 01:54:46.670
maybe you're just trying to think about it too much

2592
01:54:46.670 --> 01:54:50.120
and you really have to see what your body is telling you.

2593
01:54:50.120 --> 01:54:52.090
Because our bodies are actually giving us

2594
01:54:52.090 --> 01:54:55.930
so much information that we completely ignore.

2595
01:54:55.930 --> 01:54:58.290
And you're an expert at this.

2596
01:54:58.290 --> 01:55:00.980
Well, but athletes of all people

2597
01:55:00.980 --> 01:55:03.630
are so much more integrated in that regard,

2598
01:55:03.630 --> 01:55:05.920
like they've been trained to pay attention to their body

2599
01:55:05.920 --> 01:55:07.930
and the signals that their body is giving them.

2600
01:55:07.930 --> 01:55:10.730
So to the extent that you are still refusing

2601
01:55:10.730 --> 01:55:14.380
to pay attention to that, I think, is powerful.

2602
01:55:14.380 --> 01:55:18.250
But the greater point being that most people

2603
01:55:18.250 --> 01:55:19.880
aren't as connected to their bodies

2604
01:55:19.880 --> 01:55:21.010
in the way that athletes are.

2605
01:55:21.010 --> 01:55:23.170
So when their bodies are sending them those signals,

2606
01:55:23.170 --> 01:55:26.540
those signals are muted, or unhearable

2607
01:55:26.540 --> 01:55:30.420
because they're, clouded underneath,

2608
01:55:30.420 --> 01:55:33.120
layers of whatever else is going on with that person

2609
01:55:33.120 --> 01:55:37.591
whether they're just disconnected from that signal.

2610
01:55:37.591 --> 01:55:40.270
And I guess the question is, how do you teach somebody

2611
01:55:40.270 --> 01:55:41.530
that's disconnected from their body,

2612
01:55:41.530 --> 01:55:43.200
how to become connected to their body?

2613
01:55:43.200 --> 01:55:45.271
There's a ton of modalities,

2614
01:55:45.271 --> 01:55:47.910
but I think the real truth to that question

2615
01:55:47.910 --> 01:55:51.030
is getting to know them, and what actually

2616
01:55:51.030 --> 01:55:52.130
what their learning style is,

2617
01:55:52.130 --> 01:55:54.260
so that you can like place one of those to it.

2618
01:55:54.260 --> 01:55:56.620
'Cause I think there's different places everybody can start.

2619
01:55:56.620 --> 01:55:57.840
Some people start meditation,

2620
01:55:57.840 --> 01:55:59.490
some people start by changing diets,

2621
01:55:59.490 --> 01:56:01.250
some people start by movement,

2622
01:56:01.250 --> 01:56:02.083
so it's--
Some people need

2623
01:56:02.083 --> 01:56:05.250
spreadsheets and other people need pictures of bananas.

2624
01:56:05.250 --> 01:56:06.940
Yes, exactly.

2625
01:56:06.940 --> 01:56:08.683
There's so many ways to do this.

2626
01:56:09.969 --> 01:56:10.802
No, one way.

2627
01:56:10.802 --> 01:56:12.603
But yeah, I think that,

2628
01:56:13.848 --> 01:56:15.837
that's something I'm sort of exploring, now,

2629
01:56:15.837 --> 01:56:16.670
so a lot of people ask me that.

2630
01:56:16.670 --> 01:56:18.740
Well, I'm not in tune with my body so how am I supposed

2631
01:56:18.740 --> 01:56:20.890
to feel this somatic experience or whatever

2632
01:56:20.890 --> 01:56:24.010
if I don't even like, I don't feel anything?

2633
01:56:24.010 --> 01:56:26.420
How has the last two years changed

2634
01:56:26.420 --> 01:56:29.193
how you how you mentor these young athletes?

2635
01:56:30.120 --> 01:56:31.400
I love that question.

2636
01:56:31.400 --> 01:56:33.580
I think we've incorporated a lot more visualization

2637
01:56:33.580 --> 01:56:35.010
and imagery, work and breath work

2638
01:56:35.010 --> 01:56:36.783
into our program, which is huge.

2639
01:56:39.090 --> 01:56:42.510
Truth be told Rebecca, and I only work with two now, each

2640
01:56:42.510 --> 01:56:45.610
because of we have like 35 mentors.

2641
01:56:45.610 --> 01:56:47.610
So we sort of have to run the business side of it

2642
01:56:47.610 --> 01:56:49.700
instead of just mentoring.

2643
01:56:49.700 --> 01:56:51.938
But my specific athletes,

2644
01:56:51.938 --> 01:56:54.060
it's changed and that we have conversations

2645
01:56:54.060 --> 01:56:56.860
about what's showing up in their body.

2646
01:56:56.860 --> 01:56:58.760
And they're able to, every time they do it,

2647
01:56:58.760 --> 01:57:00.040
they get better and better.

2648
01:57:00.040 --> 01:57:02.700
At first, it's like, I don't know, I'm sore.

2649
01:57:02.700 --> 01:57:04.927
I don't know, my right shoulder is kind of sore

2650
01:57:04.927 --> 01:57:06.570
from 700 butterfly did yesterday.

2651
01:57:06.570 --> 01:57:11.570
And now it's more I was really short of breath yesterday,

2652
01:57:12.054 --> 01:57:13.297
'cause I was super stressed,

2653
01:57:13.297 --> 01:57:14.860
because I had a fight with my boyfriend

2654
01:57:14.860 --> 01:57:16.310
and I noticed they stopped breathing.

2655
01:57:16.310 --> 01:57:17.633
So it's like cool cue.

2656
01:57:18.510 --> 01:57:19.510
And we work on that.

2657
01:57:20.612 --> 01:57:21.607
And then they take that and they apply it

2658
01:57:21.607 --> 01:57:23.250
to their competition and to school.

2659
01:57:23.250 --> 01:57:25.390
It's, against the thing that runs across,

2660
01:57:25.390 --> 01:57:28.013
like, how can that work in multiple environments.

2661
01:57:30.140 --> 01:57:31.540
But it has increased awareness,

2662
01:57:31.540 --> 01:57:33.410
it's increase awareness for all of our mentors,

2663
01:57:33.410 --> 01:57:35.990
the mind body aspect in general.

2664
01:57:35.990 --> 01:57:40.300
Knowing that working on an athlete's mind, isn't it,

2665
01:57:40.300 --> 01:57:42.640
you have to really work on what they feel in their body,

2666
01:57:42.640 --> 01:57:45.760
what's showing up, and how to speak to their body

2667
01:57:45.760 --> 01:57:49.306
in a way that they can not only become more aware of it

2668
01:57:49.306 --> 01:57:50.290
and know what it needs, but in a way

2669
01:57:50.290 --> 01:57:53.230
that they can create worth through their actual being

2670
01:57:53.230 --> 01:57:55.730
so that it is aligned with their mind.

2671
01:57:55.730 --> 01:57:57.400
And they find that happening together

2672
01:57:57.400 --> 01:57:59.640
and things start to click, it's like,

2673
01:57:59.640 --> 01:58:00.990
oh, I feel less tense,

2674
01:58:00.990 --> 01:58:03.500
or I felt really relaxed going into that race.

2675
01:58:03.500 --> 01:58:04.790
What did that feel like?

2676
01:58:04.790 --> 01:58:07.210
Oh, my shoulders were down and I felt like I could breathe.

2677
01:58:07.210 --> 01:58:10.550
And yeah, I felt, so they're recognizing

2678
01:58:10.550 --> 01:58:12.640
what's happening in their system.

2679
01:58:12.640 --> 01:58:15.610
Which, if we're gonna change generations in sport,

2680
01:58:15.610 --> 01:58:17.960
you can't just tell them to think about things.

2681
01:58:19.340 --> 01:58:24.320
Sure you can but in my personal opinion, and experience,

2682
01:58:24.320 --> 01:58:26.133
I've never seen an athlete,

2683
01:58:27.020 --> 01:58:28.420
even if they love spreadsheets,

2684
01:58:28.420 --> 01:58:30.430
and love splits and times, like my brother

2685
01:58:30.430 --> 01:58:32.693
not be able to tune into their body,

2686
01:58:33.750 --> 01:58:35.490
in a time when they need to and understand

2687
01:58:35.490 --> 01:58:36.990
what's going on what it's telling them

2688
01:58:36.990 --> 01:58:39.066
what information that's giving them.

2689
01:58:39.066 --> 01:58:42.110
And to be able to do that under pressure,

2690
01:58:42.110 --> 01:58:43.910
or in a high stress environment

2691
01:58:43.910 --> 01:58:47.250
where your thinking brain isn't gonna cut it.

2692
01:58:47.250 --> 01:58:49.060
Yeah, you have to.

2693
01:58:49.060 --> 01:58:51.870
Yeah, because your body is gonna tell you first

2694
01:58:51.870 --> 01:58:53.920
what's going on always.

2695
01:58:53.920 --> 01:58:56.680
And that's the crazy thing is if we listen close enough,

2696
01:58:56.680 --> 01:58:59.470
and if we put in the reps, everything is reps,

2697
01:58:59.470 --> 01:59:02.120
reps, reps, reps, you just gotta keep putting in the reps

2698
01:59:02.120 --> 01:59:03.460
before you realize it.

2699
01:59:03.460 --> 01:59:06.110
But if you listen close enough, you're like,

2700
01:59:06.110 --> 01:59:08.223
I'm super jittery, like before this race,

2701
01:59:09.890 --> 01:59:14.610
my stomach hurts, my rib hurts,

2702
01:59:14.610 --> 01:59:17.010
all these things that will give you information.

2703
01:59:17.010 --> 01:59:18.800
Well, why do those things hurt?

2704
01:59:18.800 --> 01:59:20.403
What are you holding on to?

2705
01:59:21.290 --> 01:59:22.700
A lot of swimmers stomach hurt.

2706
01:59:22.700 --> 01:59:25.550
A lot of performers always claim,

2707
01:59:25.550 --> 01:59:27.800
they'll throw up before races, their stomach hurt,

2708
01:59:27.800 --> 01:59:29.451
those things are telling you something,

2709
01:59:29.451 --> 01:59:31.306
it's information, it's not bad

2710
01:59:31.306 --> 01:59:32.930
it's just information.

2711
01:59:32.930 --> 01:59:35.150
It's difficult to figure out what's meaningful

2712
01:59:35.150 --> 01:59:35.983
out of that too.

2713
01:59:35.983 --> 01:59:39.210
Because as you know, you're used to beating your body up

2714
01:59:39.210 --> 01:59:40.520
for so long during training

2715
01:59:40.520 --> 01:59:42.960
and then you go into this taper phase,

2716
01:59:42.960 --> 01:59:44.560
and then you're just hyper aware

2717
01:59:44.560 --> 01:59:46.850
of every little niggle in your body

2718
01:59:46.850 --> 01:59:48.580
and you're like, there's something wrong

2719
01:59:48.580 --> 01:59:51.283
because my toe hurts or something,

2720
01:59:52.772 --> 01:59:53.605
and you gotta just be like, no,

2721
01:59:53.605 --> 01:59:55.100
you're just nervous, right?

2722
01:59:55.100 --> 01:59:56.250
There's nothing wrong with you.

2723
01:59:56.250 --> 01:59:58.830
You're just hyper aware you're being hyper vigilant

2724
01:59:58.830 --> 02:00:01.500
because you've put so much time into preparing

2725
02:00:01.500 --> 02:00:03.870
for the very specific moment.

2726
02:00:03.870 --> 02:00:06.670
And everything in your in your world

2727
02:00:06.670 --> 02:00:09.060
in your experience is super heightened.

2728
02:00:09.060 --> 02:00:12.290
So true 'cause the amount of times I was told,

2729
02:00:12.290 --> 02:00:13.980
don't pay attention on how you feel.

2730
02:00:13.980 --> 02:00:16.510
Or don't worry about it if you hurt

2731
02:00:16.510 --> 02:00:17.520
or don't think about it,

2732
02:00:17.520 --> 02:00:19.120
don't think about how you feel.

2733
02:00:19.120 --> 02:00:20.791
And it was so foreign to me.

2734
02:00:20.791 --> 02:00:21.624
I was like, What do you mean?

2735
02:00:21.624 --> 02:00:23.560
That's all I do is I feel I don't understand like,

2736
02:00:23.560 --> 02:00:26.470
how am I not supposed to think about how I feel?

2737
02:00:26.470 --> 02:00:28.220
But I you nailed it with that

2738
02:00:28.220 --> 02:00:29.980
is it you become so hyper aware

2739
02:00:29.980 --> 02:00:31.363
that how can you reframe whatever it is

2740
02:00:31.363 --> 02:00:36.363
that you're feeling in your system as an okay thing,

2741
02:00:36.380 --> 02:00:38.780
as something that's just giving you information,

2742
02:00:38.780 --> 02:00:41.540
accepting it, the practice of acceptance,

2743
02:00:41.540 --> 02:00:43.801
if you're at a race or whatever,

2744
02:00:43.801 --> 02:00:44.634
and your right knee hurts,

2745
02:00:44.634 --> 02:00:45.467
but you're behind the blocks.

2746
02:00:45.467 --> 02:00:47.160
Well, not a lot you can do now.

2747
02:00:47.160 --> 02:00:49.390
So reps of doing that in practice,

2748
02:00:49.390 --> 02:00:52.170
reps of doing that with a sports site consultant,

2749
02:00:52.170 --> 02:00:54.030
reps of doing that with your coach, like,

2750
02:00:54.030 --> 02:00:55.380
what is it that means?

2751
02:00:55.380 --> 02:00:58.250
How can I reframe whatever it is in that moment,

2752
02:00:58.250 --> 02:01:00.930
through injury or through pain

2753
02:01:00.930 --> 02:01:04.900
that I can then use toward whatever I need to get done,

2754
02:01:04.900 --> 02:01:08.040
and then address it after if it's something serious,

2755
02:01:08.040 --> 02:01:10.010
when it comes like injury and whatnot.

2756
02:01:10.010 --> 02:01:13.410
But yeah, that whole field of injury psychology

2757
02:01:13.410 --> 02:01:15.110
is really cool.

2758
02:01:15.110 --> 02:01:17.190
You should pick (indistinct) brain on that sometime.

2759
02:01:17.190 --> 02:01:20.613
Yeah, I've never spoken about that specifically with--

2760
02:01:20.613 --> 02:01:21.930
It's a whole deal.

2761
02:01:21.930 --> 02:01:24.030
It's for sure, it's really interesting.

2762
02:01:24.030 --> 02:01:25.070
Like when I was in grad school,

2763
02:01:25.070 --> 02:01:26.553
Do you guys hang out?

2764
02:01:26.553 --> 02:01:28.320
We used to work out together.

2765
02:01:28.320 --> 02:01:30.438
And then he started a different gym routine.

2766
02:01:30.438 --> 02:01:32.003
He came to my gym.

2767
02:01:33.350 --> 02:01:34.310
We were buddies.

2768
02:01:34.310 --> 02:01:36.730
I see him, at source cafe every now and then.

2769
02:01:36.730 --> 02:01:39.160
He is the best, he doesn't like neighbors down there.

2770
02:01:39.160 --> 02:01:41.690
Yeah, he's great, I loved Durey.

2771
02:01:41.690 --> 02:01:43.840
We've always just had like a great rapport.

2772
02:01:45.734 --> 02:01:47.640
But yeah, that field is really cool.

2773
02:01:47.640 --> 02:01:50.980
Well, I wanna talk about your relationship to sport now

2774
02:01:50.980 --> 02:01:54.154
because if you scroll through your Instagram,

2775
02:01:54.154 --> 02:01:57.690
you're getting after it, whether it's CrossFit,

2776
02:01:57.690 --> 02:01:59.663
or like swimming in the ocean, like,

2777
02:02:00.650 --> 02:02:04.350
you still have this profound love for movement

2778
02:02:04.350 --> 02:02:07.350
and fitness, but what's interesting

2779
02:02:07.350 --> 02:02:09.010
is that it's completely outside

2780
02:02:09.010 --> 02:02:11.070
of any competitive context, right?

2781
02:02:11.070 --> 02:02:14.700
Like, I almost feel like, like,

2782
02:02:14.700 --> 02:02:18.370
it was a blessing that you didn't go and do Otillo.

2783
02:02:18.370 --> 02:02:20.620
Because you're not supposed to be,

2784
02:02:20.620 --> 02:02:22.400
your relationship to sport isn't supposed

2785
02:02:22.400 --> 02:02:25.590
to be about competition, even if you could have done that,

2786
02:02:25.590 --> 02:02:27.730
from a healthy perspective of not really caring,

2787
02:02:27.730 --> 02:02:30.180
like about how well you did

2788
02:02:30.180 --> 02:02:31.560
and just enjoying the experience.

2789
02:02:31.560 --> 02:02:34.890
I think there's something beautiful and instructive

2790
02:02:34.890 --> 02:02:39.540
about how you've completely reframed your relationship

2791
02:02:39.540 --> 02:02:43.790
to sport so that it has nothing to do with any metric.

2792
02:02:43.790 --> 02:02:45.240
Other than like, joy.

2793
02:02:45.240 --> 02:02:46.073
Exactly.

2794
02:02:47.570 --> 02:02:50.120
So it's interesting, I started to wanna be a student

2795
02:02:50.120 --> 02:02:51.940
of different things.

2796
02:02:51.940 --> 02:02:53.600
I'm very curious.

2797
02:02:53.600 --> 02:02:55.490
I wanted to try different things

2798
02:02:55.490 --> 02:02:57.100
because after I broke my heels,

2799
02:02:57.100 --> 02:03:00.180
I couldn't really do endurance things like run and whatnot.

2800
02:03:00.180 --> 02:03:03.340
Like I used to me, that was what I needed to get done

2801
02:03:03.340 --> 02:03:05.800
when I retired, right, run, run, run, run, run

2802
02:03:05.800 --> 02:03:06.633
and keep running.

2803
02:03:06.633 --> 02:03:07.640
And I love running.

2804
02:03:07.640 --> 02:03:10.150
But I was like, let's see what's possible.

2805
02:03:10.150 --> 02:03:11.910
Let's see what's possible with your body.

2806
02:03:11.910 --> 02:03:13.930
And things great as long as you're running towards

2807
02:03:13.930 --> 02:03:16.243
something and not away.
Away yes.

2808
02:03:18.405 --> 02:03:19.238
I'm just yes.

2809
02:03:19.238 --> 02:03:20.498
I'm so obsessed with running.

2810
02:03:20.498 --> 02:03:21.590
Running awesome for running away from stuff.

2811
02:03:21.590 --> 02:03:24.150
Yeah, running's great once you're running away oh yeah.

2812
02:03:24.150 --> 02:03:25.663
It was fast as hell yeah.

2813
02:03:27.860 --> 02:03:29.440
So I started getting curious.

2814
02:03:29.440 --> 02:03:32.350
And I started thinking, Okay, Caroline,

2815
02:03:32.350 --> 02:03:36.170
you did the same thing for ever.

2816
02:03:36.170 --> 02:03:37.860
Let's see what's possible.

2817
02:03:37.860 --> 02:03:40.320
And let's test the boundaries a little bit

2818
02:03:40.320 --> 02:03:43.410
and see what your body can handle what it can't,

2819
02:03:43.410 --> 02:03:45.510
