So maybe a good way to end it is

3073
02:15:10.390 --> 02:15:15.030
to share a little bit or impart a little bit

3074
02:15:15.030 --> 02:15:19.060
of wisdom or experience to the younger athlete

3075
02:15:19.060 --> 02:15:23.100
who's tuning in, who perhaps is feeling like their worth

3076
02:15:23.100 --> 02:15:25.760
is being measured by the extent to which

3077
02:15:25.760 --> 02:15:30.160
they're able to perform or who feels like they're not able

3078
02:15:30.160 --> 02:15:32.740
to be themselves completely

3079
02:15:32.740 --> 02:15:35.150
in whatever lane they've chosen right now,

3080
02:15:35.150 --> 02:15:36.460
and is trying to figure out how

3081
02:15:36.460 --> 02:15:39.090
to have a healthier relationship to,

3082
02:15:39.090 --> 02:15:42.120
maybe it's sport, but maybe it's some other thing

3083
02:15:42.120 --> 02:15:44.163
that they're involved in.

3084
02:15:45.560 --> 02:15:46.660
Well, there's two things.

3085
02:15:46.660 --> 02:15:49.700
One is that you can be feeling,

3086
02:15:49.700 --> 02:15:51.210
it's okay to feel that way.

3087
02:15:51.210 --> 02:15:52.730
Your feelings are valid.

3088
02:15:52.730 --> 02:15:56.760
I think that is very important for a young athlete to feel,

3089
02:15:56.760 --> 02:15:59.870
your feelings are valid, they're not right or wrong.

3090
02:15:59.870 --> 02:16:02.160
There's they're not measured.

3091
02:16:02.160 --> 02:16:05.100
But learning how to use them constructively.

3092
02:16:05.100 --> 02:16:06.370
Whether it's through sharing

3093
02:16:06.370 --> 02:16:08.240
or understanding it communicating,

3094
02:16:08.240 --> 02:16:10.140
and being able to use those and move forward

3095
02:16:10.140 --> 02:16:12.710
with whatever that is the key.

3096
02:16:12.710 --> 02:16:15.860
So I think we get wrapped up in not saying anything,

3097
02:16:15.860 --> 02:16:17.960
'cause we're afraid upset somebody.

3098
02:16:17.960 --> 02:16:19.540
But if there's somebody that you can share

3099
02:16:19.540 --> 02:16:23.680
how you feel with and that feels like a safe space for you,

3100
02:16:23.680 --> 02:16:25.670
feel safe to validate your feelings,

3101
02:16:25.670 --> 02:16:27.130
say it's okay, you feel that way,

3102
02:16:27.130 --> 02:16:29.090
let's get a little more information about that.

3103
02:16:29.090 --> 02:16:31.120
What is it that's really showing up there

3104
02:16:31.120 --> 02:16:35.943
and really understanding that the human's heart first.

3105
02:16:37.093 --> 02:16:37.926
They're gonna be able to perform better,

3106
02:16:37.926 --> 02:16:39.090
they're gonna be able to take that

3107
02:16:39.090 --> 02:16:40.500
and use whatever that is

3108
02:16:40.500 --> 02:16:43.150
and turn it into something constructive.

3109
02:16:43.150 --> 02:16:46.170
Because I think we we get stuck in our feelings,

3110
02:16:46.170 --> 02:16:47.960
and we get stuck just thinking they don't matter,

3111
02:16:47.960 --> 02:16:50.030
brushing them away, pushing them away, really,

3112
02:16:50.030 --> 02:16:52.102
there's so much power in it,

3113
02:16:52.102 --> 02:16:54.760
there's so much information to be had in that,

3114
02:16:54.760 --> 02:16:57.610
that's beautiful, regardless of if they're positive

3115
02:16:57.610 --> 02:17:01.990
or negative, you can take that remold it and turn it

3116
02:17:01.990 --> 02:17:04.980
into an amazing performance,

3117
02:17:04.980 --> 02:17:07.480
grade on a test relationship with somebody

3118
02:17:07.480 --> 02:17:10.350
with your family members, extra curricular,

3119
02:17:10.350 --> 02:17:13.100
whatever it is that that person's wanting to do.

3120
02:17:13.100 --> 02:17:15.280
So that's something I like to say,

3121
02:17:15.280 --> 02:17:18.410
'cause I think we're shameful of our feelings.

3122
02:17:18.410 --> 02:17:20.500
We're shameful of what that means.

3123
02:17:20.500 --> 02:17:21.847
There's nothing wrong with that.

3124
02:17:21.847 --> 02:17:23.470
It's just information.

3125
02:17:23.470 --> 02:17:25.410
And I wish I would have known that.

3126
02:17:26.328 --> 02:17:27.161
I wish I would have been okay,

3127
02:17:27.161 --> 02:17:28.760
knowing that however I felt was okay.

3128
02:17:28.760 --> 02:17:31.460
And then it wasn't there anything wrong with it,

3129
02:17:31.460 --> 02:17:33.431
it was just information.

3130
02:17:33.431 --> 02:17:34.952
Yeah, that's beautiful.

3131
02:17:34.952 --> 02:17:35.785
I think it's super important.

3132
02:17:35.785 --> 02:17:38.890
I feel like, at least in the context of sport,

3133
02:17:38.890 --> 02:17:41.230
there has been a lot of progress and movement

3134
02:17:41.230 --> 02:17:42.063
in the right direction

3135
02:17:42.063 --> 02:17:45.830
in terms of better understanding that aspect of it.

3136
02:17:45.830 --> 02:17:48.170
I mean, I'm two generations older than you,

3137
02:17:48.170 --> 02:17:51.660
but when I see, the way that young athletes

3138
02:17:51.660 --> 02:17:53.560
are being coached and mentored now,

3139
02:17:53.560 --> 02:17:55.791
compared to what it was like, when I was a kid,

3140
02:17:55.791 --> 02:17:57.010
I mean, that was long time ago.

3141
02:17:57.010 --> 02:17:59.750
But, of course, much more,

3142
02:17:59.750 --> 02:18:01.740
there's much more to be gleaned and learned.

3143
02:18:01.740 --> 02:18:04.640
Totally mental health is at the forefront right now.

3144
02:18:04.640 --> 02:18:07.640
People are caring about how people feel.

3145
02:18:07.640 --> 02:18:12.640
And I know this is an important thing to note

3146
02:18:13.660 --> 02:18:18.660
is that you can be struggling, and also be okay

3147
02:18:19.440 --> 02:18:20.570
with your performances.

3148
02:18:20.570 --> 02:18:23.630
You can admit that you're having a hard time

3149
02:18:23.630 --> 02:18:25.800
and also you'll, you'll still be okay,

3150
02:18:25.800 --> 02:18:28.920
you can still be and do great things.

3151
02:18:28.920 --> 02:18:32.777
I think there's a misunderstanding there

3152
02:18:34.540 --> 02:18:36.970
that if I, again, back to that,

3153
02:18:36.970 --> 02:18:39.830
if I share that I'm depressed

3154
02:18:39.830 --> 02:18:44.800
or having a hard time or going through something,

3155
02:18:44.800 --> 02:18:45.880
then that means

3156
02:18:47.690 --> 02:18:48.523
It's gonna--
Be well.

3157
02:18:48.523 --> 02:18:50.240
Impinge on your performance, right?

3158
02:18:50.240 --> 02:18:51.073
I mean, that's the whole message

3159
02:18:51.073 --> 02:18:52.463
of the weight of gold, right?

3160
02:18:52.463 --> 02:18:54.070
It's like kind of a call to action

3161
02:18:54.070 --> 02:18:58.500
to embrace that aspect of what it means to be vulnerable

3162
02:18:58.500 --> 02:19:02.730
and to have the courage to raise your hand and ask for help.

3163
02:19:02.730 --> 02:19:04.530
The shrouding of it, the hiding of it,

3164
02:19:04.530 --> 02:19:09.420
because you're supposed to be this bulletproof individual

3165
02:19:09.420 --> 02:19:13.000
is not in service to anybody, and certainly not yourself.

3166
02:19:13.000 --> 02:19:16.090
And it's not complaining, it's owning,

3167
02:19:16.090 --> 02:19:17.223
it's self ownership.

3168
02:19:18.852 --> 02:19:21.330
I think there's a difference between complaining

3169
02:19:21.330 --> 02:19:23.780
I have some athletes say, well, I wanna complain.

3170
02:19:25.090 --> 02:19:28.600
It's if we can shift it to itself ownership,

3171
02:19:28.600 --> 02:19:30.770
then we can take that and use it.

3172
02:19:30.770 --> 02:19:33.010
Just because you're having a hard time

3173
02:19:33.010 --> 02:19:34.310
have asked for help, et cetera

3174
02:19:34.310 --> 02:19:37.210
it doesn't mean you're all the sudden gonna perform poorly.

3175
02:19:37.210 --> 02:19:38.940
It doesn't mean that you're not focusing

3176
02:19:38.940 --> 02:19:41.310
on your swimming or your baseball or whatever,

3177
02:19:41.310 --> 02:19:43.970
it means that you're doing something for your mental health,

3178
02:19:43.970 --> 02:19:47.930
which will then help that so it's a perspective shift.

3179
02:19:47.930 --> 02:19:51.810
It does require some level of mind-body integration,

3180
02:19:51.810 --> 02:19:53.940
though because you have to know when you

3181
02:19:53.940 --> 02:19:57.470
are copping out like am I just am I just one thing out,

3182
02:19:57.470 --> 02:20:02.470
or am I really in jeopardy where I need some help?

3183
02:20:02.820 --> 02:20:03.730
There is a difference.

3184
02:20:03.730 --> 02:20:06.933
And if you don't have that kind of intuition,

3185
02:20:08.318 --> 02:20:12.790
then you might be just, indulging in your laziness,

3186
02:20:12.790 --> 02:20:15.500
instead of really being imperil.

3187
02:20:15.500 --> 02:20:19.170
But that's where great coaches and mentors come in.

3188
02:20:19.170 --> 02:20:20.990
Because if somebody is vulnerable enough

3189
02:20:20.990 --> 02:20:24.360
to share whatever it is, then they can catch that,

3190
02:20:24.360 --> 02:20:27.610
and be able to change that and turn that into something.

3191
02:20:27.610 --> 02:20:30.990
Otherwise, they will just sit in their shit,

3192
02:20:30.990 --> 02:20:33.850
so to speak, and, let it go to shit.

3193
02:20:33.850 --> 02:20:36.023
And well whatever, I'm just copping out.

3194
02:20:36.870 --> 02:20:39.170
So if they can articulate that,

3195
02:20:39.170 --> 02:20:42.970
communicate that information to whomever, coach mentor.

3196
02:20:42.970 --> 02:20:45.900
And this is where coaches and mentors can hear that,

3197
02:20:45.900 --> 02:20:48.890
taking that information and being able to help somebody,

3198
02:20:48.890 --> 02:20:52.070
being able to identify it without shame,

3199
02:20:52.070 --> 02:20:54.000
and turn it into something better.

3200
02:20:54.000 --> 02:20:56.120
Call them out on what it is, in a nice way,

3201
02:20:56.120 --> 02:20:58.590
in a beautiful way, like, hey you're tough,

3202
02:20:58.590 --> 02:20:59.760
let's make something out of this,

3203
02:20:59.760 --> 02:21:01.780
we're not gonna let this happen to you here.

3204
02:21:01.780 --> 02:21:05.150
That's where things can shift for the positive.

3205
02:21:05.150 --> 02:21:07.280
'Cause you're changing the behavior

3206
02:21:07.280 --> 02:21:09.240
through let's act on this.

3207
02:21:09.240 --> 02:21:11.970
Let's move through this, let's not tell you what's wrong,

3208
02:21:11.970 --> 02:21:14.163
and just make you sit in it longer.

3209
02:21:15.395 --> 02:21:17.190
Let's, make some change here,

3210
02:21:17.190 --> 02:21:18.890
let's do something and that's on you.

3211
02:21:18.890 --> 02:21:20.900
You're the one athlete, you're the one that needs

3212
02:21:20.900 --> 02:21:22.500
to make the change I'm here to guide you.

3213
02:21:22.500 --> 02:21:26.470
Yeah, well, I think that responsibility,

3214
02:21:26.470 --> 02:21:28.130
like we're kind of talking about it

3215
02:21:28.130 --> 02:21:30.920
from the perspective of the athlete,

3216
02:21:30.920 --> 02:21:32.610
what their responsibility is,

3217
02:21:32.610 --> 02:21:36.110
but that responsibility also rests on the coach

3218
02:21:36.110 --> 02:21:37.980
to create an environment that's conducive

3219
02:21:37.980 --> 02:21:40.140
and safe for that person to do that.

3220
02:21:40.140 --> 02:21:45.140
And I think that this is applicable outside of sport

3221
02:21:45.240 --> 02:21:49.420
in the workplace, like a boss, employee relationship,

3222
02:21:49.420 --> 02:21:51.100
or how management is structured so

3223
02:21:51.100 --> 02:21:55.420
that the work staff feels they can, raise certain issues,

3224
02:21:55.420 --> 02:21:57.730
and the manager is creating an environment

3225
02:21:57.730 --> 02:21:59.000
that's conducive to that.

3226
02:21:59.000 --> 02:22:01.670
I think, ultimately leads to a much more

3227
02:22:01.670 --> 02:22:04.430
effective healthy place to work

3228
02:22:04.430 --> 02:22:08.812
or environment to excel as an athlete.

3229
02:22:08.812 --> 02:22:11.310
Absolutely, and that is one of the most important things

3230
02:22:11.310 --> 02:22:15.090
that I think any organization can hold, coaches, teams,

3231
02:22:15.090 --> 02:22:17.790
USA Swimming, is that if the standard is held there,

3232
02:22:17.790 --> 02:22:20.130
and if people are all believing

3233
02:22:20.130 --> 02:22:23.560
in whatever leadership there is, and the leaders are able

3234
02:22:23.560 --> 02:22:27.420
to develop these people, athletes, employees,

3235
02:22:27.420 --> 02:22:31.100
whatever it is into a space of vulnerability, openness,

3236
02:22:31.100 --> 02:22:33.980
and action on what it is that we're doing,

3237
02:22:33.980 --> 02:22:35.660
not just talking about it and sitting around,

3238
02:22:35.660 --> 02:22:37.510
it's like actually acting on it,

3239
02:22:37.510 --> 02:22:39.860
whether that action is let's sit with this for a minute.

3240
02:22:39.860 --> 02:22:41.490
Or that action is let's take action

3241
02:22:41.490 --> 02:22:42.930
and do something right now.

3242
02:22:42.930 --> 02:22:45.710
Both of those things are beautiful.

3243
02:22:45.710 --> 02:22:48.240
That's how things develop.

3244
02:22:48.240 --> 02:22:52.550
And yeah, those are my greatest learnings from Mike De Boer,

3245
02:22:52.550 --> 02:22:56.130
is he was just very much either like, okay, let's,

3246
02:22:56.130 --> 02:22:58.310
now that we have that information,

3247
02:22:58.310 --> 02:23:01.130
let's either go this way and act on it immediately.

3248
02:23:01.130 --> 02:23:03.290
Or I'm gonna let you sit with that for a second.

3249
02:23:03.290 --> 02:23:05.295
I'm here right here next to you,

3250
02:23:05.295 --> 02:23:07.454
but I'm gonna let you sit with that in a second.

3251
02:23:07.454 --> 02:23:09.830
And like, knowing that I was like, held in that space,

3252
02:23:09.830 --> 02:23:12.110
I think, reflecting back that makes all the difference,

3253
02:23:12.110 --> 02:23:14.310
'cause either ways in action

3254
02:23:14.310 --> 02:23:16.450
you're giving you're empowering them either way.

3255
02:23:16.450 --> 02:23:18.160
I gotta figure it out on their own either way,

3256
02:23:18.160 --> 02:23:19.350
but it's the person that's

3257
02:23:19.350 --> 02:23:20.800
gonna hold steady and sturdy there

3258
02:23:20.800 --> 02:23:23.260
that's holding a leadership standard.

3259
02:23:23.260 --> 02:23:24.450
That you believe in that.

3260
02:23:24.450 --> 02:23:25.333
Last thing.

3261
02:23:27.760 --> 02:23:29.890
